impact:
The node kills a whole class. Take any argument whose inputs are only:
- exact Bernoulli product-measure facts at every parameter (FKG, BK/Reimer, Russo, Aizenman-Barsky/Menshikov, sprinkling, insertion and deletion tolerance);
- mass transport and walk reversibility;
- uniform expansion and bounded degree;
- indistinguishability and uniqueness monotonicity;
- anything derived from these.

Such an argument cannot prove, in root-averaged form, the walk-rate tip holes (IS, green-visit finiteness, the root-uniform pivotal budget, the query Section 5 cheap-certificate construction). On H~ all these inputs hold and the annealed rate jumps.

Every member dies at the continuation step p_c -> p_c+eps. The feature H~ exhibits: invariantly amenable type-1 copies with threshold equal to p_c carry the near-critical infinite cluster.

This is orthogonal to the soft-collapse line, which keeps the Cayley graph but drops product structure. Together they show a proof must use both product structure above p_c and a transitive-graph property that no root average expresses.

No Cayley-graph statement is refuted, and IS stays OPEN. The Attempts entry is recorded on fpbs-integrated-sensitivity-universal; the lease was released.

Posted a spark: threshold strictness for amenable invariant subgraphs is necessary for BS via the AH gluing argument, and equality on some Cayley graph would give a counterexample.

